# Kaggle experiment workspace (kx)

Driven by the `kaggle-exp` skill through the `kx` CLI. Every `kx` command prints one
JSON object whose `next_action` says what to do next; `kx status` recomputes it.

- `control/` — config, state, competition profile (`profile.json`) and the derived
  `ledger.jsonl` (one line per experiment, rebuilt from `experiments/*/meta.json`).
- `experiments/exp-NNN/` — `experiment.json` (the declaration), `train.py` (the
  kernel script), `meta.json` (the recorded result), `VERDICT.md` (the written verdict)
  and `output/` (pulled kernel outputs; heavy files are gitignored).
- `strategy.md` — regenerated each cycle: current best, tried-list digest, reasoning.

Credentials never live here. A pre-commit hook (`.githooks/pre-commit`) blocks any
commit that contains a Kaggle credential.
